# Hand-offs, agent environments, and loops (docs/guide/how-agents.md).
title: A Ready story goes to another agent's cloud only after Detect finds it and Ensure verifies its environment; the merge gate's verdict or a failed check goes back within the cap, and loops start the same commands on a schedule in the one tool you pick
direction: down
loop: loops/*.toml: a cron schedule
host: Set up in one tool: Amp, Cursor, Claude Code, or Codex
guard: aayu hook loop:<name>: halt and budget first
cmd: build --delegate, or /codex /cursor /claude /amp
detect: agentenv.Detect: CLIs, sign-ins, clouds
ensure: agentenv.Ensure: environment verified in a clean container
recv: Receiver's cloud agent, or its CLI with --local
pr: Pull request through the merge gate
human: A person: aayu ship, or the cap's page
loop -> host
host -> guard: its schedule fires
guard -> cmd: ci-failed syncs a hand-off
cmd -> detect
detect -> ensure: cloud connected
ensure -> recv: the brief
recv -> pr
pr -> cmd: send back
pr -> human: merge-ready or capped
